@startuml
autonumber
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBorderColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5D7C
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
}

participant "Kubelet / Multus" as Multus
participant "evpn-cni" as CNI
participant "evpn-node-agent\nCNI gRPC server" as Agent
participant "Network backend\nveth / netns" as Network
participant "Endpoint manager" as Endpoint
participant "OVN NBDB" as NBDB
participant "Attachment manager\nOVS" as Attach
participant "OVN/OVS forwarding" as Forwarding
participant "Asynchronous Type-2\nreconcilers (optional)" as Exporter
participant "managed gobgpd\n(k8gobgp DaemonSet)" as GoBGP
participant "Remote workload / FRR peer" as Remote
participant "Workload A" as Workload
participant "Survivor endpoint B" as Survivor
participant "E2E test runner" as Test
participant "Containerlab E2E\nlifecycle (test only)" as Lab

== E2E laboratory (not a runtime dependency) ==
Test -> Lab : reserve exact topology; deploy native kind + FRR
Lab -> Lab : verify ownership, readiness and management CA
Lab --> Test : private kubeconfig and environment receipts
Test -> Test : deploy OVN/OVS, managed k8gobgp, Multus and node-agent
note over Test,GoBGP
  BGPConfiguration CRD -> k8gobgp reconciliation -> managed gobgpd.
  Manager and daemon share one upstream image.
  Type-2 reconcilers use local Unix GoBGP gRPC independently of CNI RPCs.
end note

== ADD ==
Multus -> CNI : ADD(container, network, attachment, workload UID)
CNI -> Agent : CNIAddRequest over Unix socket
Agent -> Agent : validate identity + map endpoint spec
Agent -> Network : Ensure attachment
Network --> Agent : host interface / attachment state
Agent -> Endpoint : EnsureEndpoint
Endpoint -> NBDB : ensure owned Logical_Switch_Port
NBDB --> Endpoint : LSP identity / state
Endpoint -> Attach : ensure identity-aware local attachment
Attach --> Endpoint : attached interface
Endpoint --> Agent : endpoint status
Agent --> CNI : success + endpoint result
CNI --> Multus : CNI result
Exporter -> Exporter : asynchronously observe authoritative local evidence
Exporter -> GoBGP : AddPath local Type-2; retain UUID (when enabled)

group Failure exits instead of the successful ADD above
alt network attachment setup fails
  Network --> Agent : error
  Agent --> CNI : explicit error
else endpoint provisioning fails
  Endpoint --> Agent : error
  Agent -> Network : delete newly created network state
  Agent -> Agent : remove failed endpoint record
  Agent --> CNI : explicit error
end
end

== CHECK (read-only) ==
Multus -> CNI : CHECK
CNI -> Agent : CNICheckRequest
Agent -> Agent : resolve exact endpoint identity
Agent -> NBDB : check LSP identity
NBDB --> Agent : matching owned identity
Agent -> Network : verify attachment
Network --> Agent : present
Agent -> Attach : verify local attachment
Attach --> Agent : present
Agent --> CNI : CHECK success / mismatch error

== Initial traffic and packet evidence ==
Workload -> Forwarding : initial workload packet
Forwarding -> Remote : OVN/OVS-forwarded VXLAN traffic
Remote --> Forwarding : reverse workload packet
Forwarding --> Workload : bidirectional connectivity
note over Forwarding,Remote
  Full-lifecycle acceptance correlates five capture points and decoded
  packets with the initial endpoint identity, VNI, VTEPs and traffic direction.
end note

== Initial DEL and withdrawal ==
Multus -> CNI : DEL(exact identity + incarnation)
CNI -> Agent : CNIDelRequest
Agent -> Agent : reject stale identity; absent DEL is idempotent
Agent -> Attach : delete matching owned attachment
Attach --> Agent : detached
Agent -> NBDB : delete matching owned LSP
NBDB --> Agent : delete accepted
Agent -> Network : delete owned network attachment
Network --> Agent : removed
Agent --> CNI : deleted / already absent
Exporter -> Exporter : asynchronously observe endpoint removal
Exporter -> GoBGP : DeletePath exact owned UUIDs (when enabled)

Multus -> CNI : repeated DEL (same identity)
CNI -> Agent : CNIDelRequest
Agent --> CNI : already absent / idempotent success
Survivor -> Forwarding : verify survivor after initial DEL
Forwarding --> Survivor : survivor traffic preserved

== Replacement on the existing network ==
Multus -> CNI : ADD(new workload UID and attachment identity)
CNI -> Agent : CNIAddRequest
Agent -> Network : Ensure replacement netns / veth attachment
Agent -> Endpoint : EnsureEndpoint(new identity)
Endpoint -> NBDB : ensure replacement Logical_Switch_Port
NBDB --> Endpoint : replacement LSP
Endpoint -> Attach : ensure replacement OVS attachment
Attach --> Endpoint : attached interface
Endpoint --> Agent : replacement endpoint status
Agent --> CNI : replacement result
CNI --> Multus : replacement CNI result
Exporter -> GoBGP : asynchronously AddPath replacement Type-2

Multus -> CNI : CHECK(replacement identity)
CNI -> Agent : CNICheckRequest
Agent -> NBDB : verify replacement LSP
Agent -> Attach : verify replacement OVS attachment
Agent --> CNI : replacement CHECK result

Workload -> Forwarding : replacement workload packet
Forwarding -> Remote : replacement VXLAN traffic
Remote --> Forwarding : reverse replacement traffic
Forwarding --> Workload : bidirectional connectivity
note over Forwarding,Remote
  Replacement captures and decoded packets are phase-prefixed and checked
  against the new endpoint identity; stale initial attribution must not pass.
end note
Survivor -> Forwarding : verify survivor after replacement ADD
Forwarding --> Survivor : survivor traffic preserved

Multus -> CNI : final DEL(replacement identity)
CNI -> Agent : CNIDelRequest
Agent -> Attach : remove owned replacement attachment
Agent -> NBDB : remove owned replacement LSP
Agent -> Network : delete owned replacement network attachment
Agent --> CNI : deleted
CNI --> Multus : DEL success
Exporter -> GoBGP : asynchronously DeletePath replacement UUIDs
Survivor -> Forwarding : verify survivor connectivity
Forwarding --> Survivor : survivor traffic preserved
Test -> Test : delete survivor through CNI; withdraw remote workload;\nwait for empty owned routes and endpoint state
Test -> NBDB : guarded ovn-nbctl ls-del of test-owned network
Test -> Test : verify foreign LSP / integration devices preserved
Test -> Lab : collect diagnostics; destroy exact owned topology
Lab --> Test : owned resources absent; unrelated resources preserved

note over NBDB
  OVN NBDB -> SBDB binding propagation is asynchronous.
  CHECK verifies endpoint identity; it is not a replacement
  for dataplane traffic tests.
end note
note over Endpoint,Attach
  Rollback depends on the failure point. If local attachment
  fails after OVN LSP creation, the current endpoint manager
  does not compensate that LSP yet. Current full-lifecycle
  evidence injects a missing network namespace before LSP
  creation; it does not establish general post-LSP compensation.
end note
note over Multus,Attach
  This sequence covers the optional Kubernetes CNI application lifecycle.
  The full-lifecycle E2E additionally checks repeated ADD/DEL, negative CHECK,
  injected pre-LSP ADD rollback, survivor preservation and guarded cleanup. OVN/OVS
  endpoint attachment is not the standalone OVSDB-Programmed EVPN dataplane.
end note
note over Exporter,GoBGP
  Optional Type-2 export/import is a separate CNI integration.
  RPC success does not wait for BGP convergence.
  This application sequence is not independent Framework
  acceptance for either integration mode.
end note
@enduml
